<article class="env-lemma" id="09JP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09JP">Lemma <span data-tag="09JP">22.5.2</span>.</a> Let $(A, \text{d})$ be a differential graded algebra. Let $f, g : L \to M$ be homomorphisms of differential graded $A$-modules. Suppose given further homomorphisms $a : K \to L$, and $c : M \to N$. If $h : L \to M$ is an $A$-module map which defines a homotopy between $f$ and $g$, then $c \circ h \circ a$ defines a homotopy between $c \circ f \circ a$ and $c \circ g \circ a$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate from Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0112" data-tag="0112">12.13.7</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>